.TH REDSTONEPANEL 8 "November 2026" "redstonepanel 1.23.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
redstonepanel \- manage the RedstonePanel Minecraft server panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redstonepanel status
.br
.B redstonepanel add-user
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-role " admin|user" ]
.br
.B redstonepanel set-name
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel reset-security
.br
.B redstonepanel reset-2fa
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel terminal
.BR on | off
.br
.B redstonepanel removed
.br
.B redstonepanel restore
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel backup
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel offsite-copy
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel offsite-key
.br
.B redstonepanel restart-server
.I NAME
.br
.B redstonepanel check-updates
.br
.B redstonepanel notify-test
.br
.B redstonepanel ports
.br
.B redstonepanel upgrade
.br
.B redstonepanel cluster
.RB { create
.IR NAME | status | join-code
.RI [ URL ]| backup
.IR FILE | promote
.IR FILE }
.br
.B redstonepanel join
.I CODE
.br
.B redstonepanel leave
.br
.B redstonepanel cluster-https
.SH DESCRIPTION
RedstonePanel is a web panel that deploys and manages Minecraft Java Edition and
Bedrock Dedicated Server instances as systemd services. Java servers can be vanilla, Paper
or Fabric, on a chosen Minecraft version, and each unit runs the Java from
.I /usr/lib/jvm
that the version needs. The package doesn't install Java: when a server needs one that
isn't installed, an admin can install its openjdk-N-jre-headless package from the panel,
and remove one that no server uses. The panel itself runs as the
.B redstonepanel
systemd service, by default at
.IR http://<server>:8080/ .
This command performs administrative tasks and must be run as root.
.PP
Supported systems: Ubuntu 24.04, 26.04 and 26.10, Linux Mint 22 and 23, Debian 13 and 64\-bit
Raspberry Pi OS (Raspberry Pi 4 or 5), on x86\-64 and ARM64 (aarch64) machines. The panel offers the
openjdk\-N\-jre\-headless versions the system's apt sources have (Debian 13: 21 and 25).
Bedrock Dedicated Server only exists for x86\-64, so on ARM64 the panel refuses to create,
import, restore, update or receive Bedrock servers and runs Java servers only. A new Java
server gets a 2 GB heap (1 GB on a machine with 3 GB of memory or less); change it on the
server's Maintenance tab (Memory and limits), which also sets optional hard memory and CPU
limits as a systemd drop\-in,
.IR /etc/systemd/system/minecraft-NAME.service.d/redstonepanel-limits.conf .
.PP
A panel account with the
.B user
role can do only what an admin allows on each server (Users > Servers in the panel: view,
console, start/stop, players, files, mods, settings, backups); the grants are kept in
.IR /var/lib/redstonepanel/grants.json .
SFTP (Panel Settings > SFTP, off by default, port 2022) lets FileZilla, WinSCP or
.BR sftp (1)
reach one server's folder per sign\-in: the user name is
.IB ACCOUNT . SERVER
with the account's password or an SSH key added under Password > SSH keys (accounts with
two\-factor sign\-in must use a key). It runs as
.BR redstonepanel\-sftp.service ,
which the panel writes, starts and stops with the setting, and needs the
.B python3\-paramiko
package. Its host key is
.IR /var/lib/redstonepanel/sftp_host_key .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show whether the service is running, its address, the HTTPS and sign\-in mode, and the panel accounts.
.TP
.BI "add-user " NAME " \fR[\fB\-\-role admin\fR|\fBuser\fR]"
Create a panel account (default role: admin). The password is asked for interactively,
or read from the first line of standard input when it is not a terminal.
.TP
.BI "set-name " NAME
Set the name the panel shows in its sidebar, browser tab and sign\-in page, to tell several
servers' panels apart (up to 40 characters; visible before signing in). An empty name
(\fB""\fR) goes back to the server's host name. Takes effect without a restart.
.TP
.B reset-security
Recovery: switch the panel back to plain HTTP on port 8080 with sign\-in required, and restart it.
On a cluster member this cuts the panel off from the cluster until
.B cluster-https
is run.
.TP
.BI "reset-2fa " NAME
Recovery: turn off two\-factor sign\-in for the panel or Linux account
.IR NAME ,
for example after a lost phone with no recovery codes left. The account signs in with its
password and can set two\-factor up again (it is asked to at once when Panel Settings require
it for admins). If
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/totp.json
can't be read, it is moved aside to
.I totp.json.damaged
instead, which turns two\-factor off for every account.
.TP
.BR terminal " on|" off
Turn the panel's terminal on or off (the same switch as Panel Settings > Terminal). When it is
on, admins open a shell on this machine from the Dashboard, over HTTPS, as a Linux account: the
one they signed in with, or one they type with its password at the terminal's login prompt.
Turning it off closes open terminals within a minute. Every terminal is written to
.IR /var/log/redstonepanel/panel.log .
.TP
.B removed
List game servers that were uninstalled with \fBKeep World\fR: folders in
.I /opt/minecraft-*
that no systemd service uses.
.TP
.BI "restore " NAME
Restore a removed server: write a new systemd service for it under the same name, keep its
port unless another server now uses it, download the server binary only if it is missing,
then enable and start it.
.TP
.BI "backup " NAME
Back up a game server now, into
.IR /var/backups/redstonepanel/NAME/ .
A running Java server stops writing to disk during the copy (over RCON), a running Bedrock
server through \fBsave hold\fR. Backups taken this way are never pruned. Each server's backup
timer, \fBredstonepanel-backup@\fINAME\fB.timer\fR, runs the same command for scheduled
backups, which keep only the number (and, if set, the number of days) set in the panel's
Backups tab. If the server's backups are copied to backup storage, the copy starts afterwards in
its own transient unit,
.BI redstonepanel\-offsite\- NAME .service ,
so a slow upload never holds the backup up.
.TP
.BI "offsite-copy " NAME
Copy a game server's backups to every backup storage (SSH or S3-compatible, set under Panel
Settings > Backup storage) that keeps them, now: every manual backup and the scheduled ones the
storage's retention keeps, each checked with SHA\-256. Old scheduled copies beyond the storage's
count or age are deleted there; the newest copy is never deleted by age.
.TP
.B offsite-key
Print this panel's SSH public key (made on first use). Add it to the
.I ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
of the user the panel signs in as on SSH backup storage.
.TP
.BI "restart-server " NAME
Warn the server's players in game (Java over RCON, Bedrock through its console), wait the
warning time set in the panel's Maintenance tab, then restart the server. A stopped server is
left stopped, and the restart waits for a running backup of the same server. Each server's
restart timer, \fBredstonepanel-restart@\fINAME\fB.timer\fR, runs this command; it fires the
warning time before the restart time shown in the panel.
.TP
.B check-updates
Look for a newer release of every game server on this machine (Bedrock Dedicated Server,
Minecraft, Paper builds and the Fabric loader; never snapshots or pre\-releases), cache what
it finds in
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/updates.json
for the panel's \fBUpdate available\fR badges, and send one webhook message per new version.
Then update the Bedrock servers whose Maintenance tab has \fBUpdate automatically\fR on: warn
players in game, wait five minutes, stop the server, take a "Before update" backup (the newest
three are kept), install the new files (its server.properties, permissions.json and
allowlist.json stay), start it and wait for "Server started.". If it doesn't start, the old
files and the world from the backup are put back and it starts on the old version; the failure
shows under Needs attention. \fBredstonepanel-updates.timer\fR runs this every 6 hours,
also while the panel is stopped. Exits 1 if an update failed.
.TP
.B notify-test
Send a test message to the webhook set under Panel Settings > Notifications.
.TP
.B ports
The Port check: list every port the game servers and the panel need, which program holds
each one now (name, process id, path, command line, its systemd unit, or its Docker
container), and the conflicts found, with what the panel does about each. Works while the
panel itself is stopped, for example when another program took its web port.
.TP
.B upgrade
Run apt-get update, then upgrade only the redstonepanel package, keeping changed
configuration files. The dashboard's Update now button runs this as the transient unit
\fBredstonepanel-upgrade.service\fR, so it carries on while the panel restarts; its output is
in \fI/var/lib/redstonepanel/upgrade.log\fR and the outcome in \fIupgrade.json\fR.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
The package installs a systemd drop-in for every
.BR minecraft-*.service ,
.IR /usr/lib/systemd/system/minecraft-.service.d/redstonepanel.conf .
It treats exit status 143 (Java stopped by SIGTERM) as a clean stop. Its \fBExecStop\fR runs
\fBredstonepanel stop-unit\fR, which types a Bedrock server's own \fBstop\fR command into its
console and waits up to 75 seconds for it to save the world and quit before systemd ends what is
left (Java saves on SIGTERM, so nothing is done for it). Every stop goes through it: the Stop and
Restart buttons, backups, restores, moves, updates, scheduled restarts and shutting the machine
down. Its \fBExecStartPost\fR and \fBExecStopPost\fR run \fBredstonepanel notify-unit\fR, which sends
"started", "stopped" and "crashed" notifications to the webhook, if one is set. They run without
the panel, so a crash is reported while the panel is stopped. Failures of these hooks never
affect the game server.
.PP
A stop that systemd was not asked for is a crash. Bedrock servers run under \fBscreen\fR, which
exits 0 when the game dies, so systemd would not restart them; when a Bedrock server's console
log doesn't end with "Quit correctly" (its \fBstop\fR command), the hook starts the server again
after 20 seconds with a transient \fBsystemd-run\fR timer.
.PP
After a crash, or a stop nobody asked for (such as a failed start), the hook also reads the
newest crash report, the end of the server's log and what it printed to the journal, names the
cause when it is a known one (missing dependency, mod or plugin for another version, wrong
Java, port in use, out of memory, EULA, damaged world) and the mod or plugin it points at, and
keeps the result in \fI/var/lib/redstonepanel/crashes/NAME.json\fR for the server's Last crash
card. The cause is added to the "crashed" notification.
.SH CLUSTER COMMANDS
A cluster lets one panel, the master, manage the game servers of other RedstonePanels, its
nodes, with every tab of each server. The master runs a small certificate authority and issues
every member's HTTPS certificate; certificates only cover private addresses and local names
(.lan, .local, .home.arpa, .internal), and the master renews them 30 days before they expire.
A master, or a node on a public address, may use its own certificate (certbot) instead.
A node accepts the master's token only for its game servers, templates and Java: never users,
settings, HTTPS, panel updates or erasing a server's files. Master admins act as admins on the
nodes and master users as users; both panels log each change as [CLUSTER] user@master.
.TP
.BI "cluster create " NAME
Make this panel the master of a new cluster, switch it to cluster HTTPS and restart it.
.TP
.B cluster status
Show this panel's role and, on a master, its nodes and pending join codes.
.TP
.BI "cluster join-code " "R[PURLR]"
On the master: print a single\-use join code, valid for one hour, and the command to run on
the new node. URL is the address nodes use to reach the master (default: its first private address).
.TP
.BI "join " CODE
Join the cluster in a join code, switch to cluster HTTPS and restart.
.TP
.B leave
On a node: leave the cluster and go back to self\-signed HTTPS (remove the node on the master too).
On a master with no nodes: dissolve the cluster.
.TP
.BI "cluster backup " FILE
On the master: write the cluster's state (CA, nodes and their tokens, panel accounts, templates)
to FILE, encrypted with a passphrase that is asked for (or read from standard input).
.TP
.BR "cluster nightly on" | off
On the master: write an encrypted cluster backup to
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/cluster/backups/
every night after 3:00, keeping 7.
.B on
asks for the passphrase, which is stored on the master;
.B off
forgets it.
.TP
.BI "cluster promote " FILE
Make this panel the master from a backup, replacing its panel accounts and templates. Nodes
accept the new master at once and refuse the old one from then on.
.TP
.B cluster-https
Turn cluster HTTPS back on after
.BR reset-security .
.SH SIGNING IN
Linux accounts in the
.B sudo
or
.B redstonepanel
group can sign in with their Linux password (checked through PAM) and are panel admins.
Panel accounts are created with
.B add-user
or by an admin in the panel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/
Panel state: users.json (scrypt password hashes), totp.json (two-factor secrets and hashed recovery codes), settings.json, secret.key, tls/, cluster/, templates and chat history.
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/cluster/
Cluster state (mode 0700): role, the cluster CA and this panel's certificate; on a master also the nodes and their tokens.
.TP
.I /var/log/redstonepanel/panel.log
Activity log shown in the panel's console.
.TP
.I /opt/minecraft-*/
Game servers. Removing or purging the package never deletes them. Admins can browse and edit
them in the panel's Files tab, which never follows symlinks and gives new files to the
folder's owner.
.TP
.I /opt/minecraft-*/.redstonepanel-server.json
A Java server's type (vanilla, paper or fabric), Minecraft version, build and the Java it
needs, written at every download.
.TP
.I /var/backups/redstonepanel/
Backups, one folder per server (mode 0700). Kept when a server is uninstalled or the package
is purged. Schedules are in /var/lib/redstonepanel/backups.json.
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/backup-targets.json
Backup storage (SSH and S3-compatible) and which servers' backups go there, including S3 secret
keys (mode 0600; never sent back to the browser). This panel's SSH key and the storage host keys
are in
.IR /var/lib/redstonepanel/ssh/ .
On the storage, copies are kept under
.IR FOLDER/PANEL\-ID/SERVER/ ,
each with a
.I .sha256
file next to it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/notifications.json
The notification webhook URL and the events to send (mode 0600: the URL lets anyone post to
the channel).
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/restarts.json
Scheduled restart times and warnings.
.TP
.I /var/lib/redstonepanel/updates.json
The last update check: newer versions found per server, failed lookups, the result of each
server's last Bedrock update, and the versions already announced. Which Bedrock servers update
themselves is in
.IR auto-updates.json .
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/redstonepanel/phantom/
The Phantom LAN proxy program (jhead/phantom, SHA\-256 checked) that Bedrock servers' Add\-ons
tab installs. Each server's proxy runs as
.BI phantom\- NAME .service
under the minecraft user. Removing or purging the package leaves them; Uninstall in the tab
or removing the server deletes a proxy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
